# source material is large binary; keep it tracked but ignore OS cruft inside
reference/**/.DS_Store

# The global ignore file (~/.gitignore_global) carries `Icon?`, the macOS
# `Icon\r` resource-fork pattern. This filesystem is case-insensitive, so that
# pattern also matches any directory named `icons` — which silently excluded the
# 84 generated icon components and the manifest PNGs from every commit.
# Re-include them explicitly. A repo .gitignore takes precedence over the global.
!src/components/ui/icons/
!public/icons/

# Conflict copies. Something in this working tree, most likely iCloud Drive
# sync, periodically duplicates files as "name 2.ts", "name 3.png". 85 of them
# were swept into a commit once already and had to be stripped out, and the same
# artefacts inside .next break `tsc` with duplicate-identifier errors that look
# like real type failures. They are never wanted.
* [0-9].*

# Source material, deliberately not in this repository.
#
# The handover brief, the competitor teardowns, the product one-pagers and the
# prior design artefacts are confidential: positioning, the SEBI compliance
# rails, the naming freeze covering unreleased tools, and the founder document.
# This repository is public, so they are kept on disk and out of every commit.
# They were removed from history before the repository was made public.
#
# See docs/README.md for how to obtain them.
/docs/00-brief/
/docs/01-inspiration/
/docs/02-product-context/
/reference/
